</section>

<section class="section-sm">
    <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head center">
            <span class="eyebrow center-line">Applications</span>
            <h2>Packing specified for the voyage</h2>
            <p>
                The examples below are representative of work we do repeatedly. Clients
                are described by sector rather than by name. Figures come from the
                consignment records we keep for each programme.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- =============================== case 01 ================================ -->
<section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="shell split wide-left reveal">
        <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Automotive Components</span>
            <h2>Bare machined castings arriving flecked with rust</h2>
            <p>
                <strong>The challenge.</strong> A tier-one automotive supplier was
                shipping machined iron castings from Nhava Sheva to Bremerhaven — a
                26-day door-to-door transit crossing the equator twice. Parts left the
                plant clean and arrived with surface corrosion in the bores. The oil
                dip they were using had to be degreased on arrival, which the customer
                had begun charging back.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>What we supplied.</strong> We moved them off oil entirely and
                onto 100-micron VCI gusseted bags, one casting per bag, heat-sealed,
                with a desiccant sachet sized to the bag volume rather than the
                container. Pallets were unitised in pre-stretched film and strapped
                over laminated edge boards so the stacks could be double-tiered.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>The outcome.</strong> Corrosion rejections went from an average
                of 4.2% of each consignment to nil across the following 14 months.
                Because the parts no longer needed degreasing, the customer dropped the
                chargeback and cut a step out of their own goods-inward process.
            </p>

            <ul class="check-list">
                <li><a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Detail" asp-route-slug="vci-anti-corrosion-film">VCI Anti-Corrosion Film</a> — 100 micron gusseted bags</li>
                <li><a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Detail" asp-route-slug="stretch-shrink-film">Stretch &amp; Shrink Film</a> — pre-stretched, 17 micron</li>
                <li><a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Detail" asp-route-slug="edge-corner-protection">Edge &amp; Corner Protection</a> — 50 mm laminated angle</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
            <div class="media-frame" style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 2rem;text-align:center;color:#fff">
                <b style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:4.4rem;line-height:1;color:var(--orange)">0%</b>
                <span style="display:block;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.8rem;margin-top:.6rem;opacity:.85">
                    Corrosion rejections
                </span>
                <p style="margin:1.4rem 0 0;font-size:.93rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,.7)">
                    Down from 4.2% per consignment, sustained across 14 months and
                    approximately 380 containers.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- =============================== case 02 ================================ -->
<section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="shell split wide-right reveal">
        <div>
            <div class="media-frame" style="background:var(--white);padding:2.6rem 2rem;border:1px solid var(--border)">
                <span class="eyebrow">At a glance</span>
                <table class="spec-table">
                    <tr><th>Lane</th><td>Mundra &rarr; Jebel Ali</td></tr>
                    <tr><th>Transit</th><td>9 days port to port</td></tr>
                    <tr><th>Equipment</th><td>40 ft HC, FCL</td></tr>
                    <tr><th>Cargo</th><td>Groundnut in jute bags</td></tr>
                    <tr><th>Desiccant load</th><td>8 &times; 1 kg poles</td></tr>
                    <tr><th>Claims after</th><td>None in 340 containers</td></tr>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Agricultural Commodities</span>
            <h2>Container rain soaking the top tier of every load</h2>
            <p>
                <strong>The challenge.</strong> A Gujarat-based agri exporter kept losing
                the top two tiers of groundnut bags to moisture. The cargo was dry at
                loading — the water was coming out of the cargo itself, condensing on
                the container roof overnight and dripping back down. Two claims in one
                quarter had put their buyer relationship at risk.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>What we supplied.</strong> We calculated the moisture load from
                the commodity's own water content and the container volume rather than
                using a rule of thumb, which gave eight 1 kg calcium chloride poles per
                40 ft high cube — roughly double what they had been using. We also
                changed the placement, hanging them along the side rails instead of
                bunching them at the doors, and added kraft dunnage bags to stop the
                stack shifting into the walls.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>The outcome.</strong> No moisture claim has been raised in the
                340 containers shipped since. The desiccant cost per container went up
                by about &#8377;900; the claims it displaced were running to several
                lakh a quarter.
            </p>

            <ul class="check-list">
                <li><a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Detail" asp-route-slug="container-desiccants">Container Desiccants</a> — 1 kg hanging poles</li>
                <li><a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Detail" asp-route-slug="dunnage-air-bags">Dunnage Air Bags</a> — Level 3 kraft, 300 mm gaps</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

